# This is a Windows-first repo with `core.autocrlf=true`, which checks text files
# out with CRLF. The timeline snapshots are written by the test suite with LF, so
# without this every snapshot assertion fails on a fresh clone — the record and the
# thing it records disagree about invisible bytes. Pinning LF in the working tree
# costs nothing: git already stores it that way.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.mp4 -text
*.mp3 -text
*.jpg -text
*.jpeg -text
*.png -text
*.ttf -text
